       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review. My instructions don't let me enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose based on a claim like that. This dose is 5,100 mg/day, and the labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day.\n\nYou have a few ways to go from here:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled maximum.** I can place one now, such as 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 1,000 mg twice daily (2,000 mg/day).\n- **Use the pharmacy or prescriber override pathway.** If the protocol is real and approved, the order can go through your hospital's process for above-maximum doses. That usually means a pharmacy-verified order or a non-formulary or protocol order set, and it leaves a documented audit trail.\n- **Check the dose with the prescriber or pharmacist.** Make sure 1700 mg three times daily is what the protocol specifies and not a transcription error.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
